# Force LF for shell/SQL scripts regardless of any individual clone's own
# core.autocrlf setting. Found live, 2026-08-25 (Pass 4, controlled-failure
# qualification): release/0.1.2/scripts/update_offline.sh had CRLF line
# endings this whole time (this Windows checkout's own core.autocrlf=true
# silently re-normalizes any working-tree LF fix back to CRLF on the next
# git operation, without a .gitattributes forcing the real, stored line
# ending) -- invisible until the RAH Offline Installation Platform first
# actually executed the file directly via its own shebang line, which the
# Linux kernel parses literally including the trailing \r
# ("env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory"). `bash -n` never catches
# this since it invokes bash directly, bypassing the shebang entirely.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
